--- Deviation notes (no silent drift) ---
1. Module path: prompt gate says ':app:' but apps/android/settings.gradle.kts maps the single
   app module to Gradle path ':android' (sources under app/). Gate run with ':android:' (the
   real, only module). ':app:' does not exist and would be a false red.
2. Native output path: prompt template 'app/src/main/java/com/teslasync/dashboard-widgets/' is
   non-compilable (real root package is io.teslasync.android; a hyphenated dir is an illegal
   Kotlin package segment). Implemented at the real, compiling location:
   apps/android/app/src/main/java/io/teslasync/android/dashboard/widgets/APIUsageWidget.*
3. Build prerequisite: the generated shared-core API layer (io.teslasync.shared.core.api.generated.*)
   is a gitignored, regenerate-not-committed-raw OpenAPI client (.gitignore L379-380 'apps/**/generated/')
   and was absent in this fresh worktree. Regenerated it via the repo's own deterministic generator
   (npx tsx@4.22.4 apps/tools/codegen/gen-clients.ts -> 10 Kotlin + 10 C# files) so the gate can
   compile -- the documented, intended build step. These artifacts stay gitignored / uncommitted.
4. Per-state Compose UI + a11y tests live in src/androidTest (instrumented, the project's
   convention for Compose tests). They compile (compileDebugAndroidTestKotlin PASS) but require
   a device/emulator to execute, so the emulator-less gate exercises them via the JVM unit
   tests (testReleaseUnitTest) which cover parse/projection/mapper/registration/diagnostics and
   the full ViewModel state matrix.

